    "title": "pandas.Index.get_indexer_for — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.get_indexer_for#\n\n- \nfinal Index.get_indexer_for(*target* )[source]#\n- Guaranteed return of an indexer even when non-unique. This dispatches to get_indexer or get_indexer_non_unique as appropriate. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **target** Index\n    - An iterable containing the values to be used for computing indexer.\n  - Returns:\n    - np.ndarray[np.intp]\n    - List of indices.\n See also \n  - `Index.get_indexer`\n  - Computes indexer and mask for new index given the current index.\n  - `Index.get_non_unique`\n  - Returns indexer and masks for new index given the current index.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index([np.nan, \"var1\", np.nan]) >>> idx.get_indexer_for([np.nan]) array([0, 2])",
    "markdown_length": 691,
